The latest device testing shows that these systems are functional, but the
construction geometry remains inconsistent around corners, angled supports, and
roof peaks.

This is a focused construction-geometry refinement.

Do not add new gameplay systems, levels, materials, projectiles, progression,
monetization, or visual fortress transformation.

PRODUCT GOAL

The construction system should recognize ordinary architectural intent.

Players should be able to create clean:

- L-shaped timber corners
- Vertical posts at horizontal beam endpoints
- Angled rafters seated on block corners
- Symmetric peaked roofs
- Asymmetric but geometrically valid roofs
- Post-and-beam frames
- Diagonal braces
- T-shaped timber frames
- Enclosed wisp chambers

The pieces should align cleanly without pixel-perfect placement.

Connections should remain physically credible:

- Connected structures should not fall apart under ordinary gravity merely
  because of tiny geometric gaps.
- Unsupported structures should still fall, pivot, spread, strain, or break.
- Joints should remain breakable.
- Snapping must not create indestructible structures.
- Physics remains authoritative after placement.

