MODULAR CONSTRUCTION UNIT

Define one authoritative world-space construction unit.

Recommended starting model:

- Standard block width: 1.0 unit
- Standard block height: 1.0 unit
- Wood block: 1.0 × 1.0 units
- Stone block: 1.0 × 1.0 units
- Bullseye Block: 1.0 × 1.0 units
- Timber Beam length: an intentional whole-number multiple of block width
- Timber Beam thickness: an intentional fraction of block height

Evaluate these two reasonable beam-length options:

OPTION A

- Timber Beam length: 2.0 units
- Timber Beam thickness: 0.25 units

OPTION B

- Timber Beam length: 3.0 units
- Timber Beam thickness: 0.25 units

Select the option that best preserves the current battlefield, inventory value,
mobile manipulation, and accepted structures.

Do not select a ratio based only on the current artwork.

Document the selected ratio and why it is appropriate.

The selected system must provide predictable relationships such as:

- A known number of block widths equals one beam length.
- Beam thickness is an exact fraction of block height.
- Sockets use exact local-space coordinates.
- Face and corner geometry derive from the same dimensions.
- Collider geometry and visible geometry agree.

