ACCEPTANCE SCENARIOS

A. MODULAR SPAN

- Place standard blocks in a row.
- Place one Timber Beam above them.
- Confirm the selected modular ratio is visually and geometrically exact.
- Confirm no accumulating unexplained gap.

B. VERTICAL-TO-HORIZONTAL CORNER

- Place a horizontal beam.
- Bring a vertical beam to its left end.
- Confirm clean L-corner preview.
- Commit.
- Repeat at the right end.
- Confirm mirrored result.

C. REVERSE CORNER ORDER

- Place vertical first, horizontal second.
- Confirm the same resulting seam and joint.

D. ANGLED RAFTER ON BLOCK CORNER

- Place a wall block.
- Rotate a rafter to 45 degrees.
- Approach the upper inner corner.
- Confirm Corner Seat or Corner Joint preview.
- Confirm no pull toward a farther face-center candidate.
- Commit and test.

E. SYMMETRIC PEAKED ROOF

- Build equal-height supports.
- Use equal and opposite rafter angles.
- Seat lower endpoints at corresponding corners.
- Join upper endpoints.
- Confirm shared centered apex.
- Confirm both lower supports recognized.
- Test stability.
- Confirm roof remains assembled under ordinary gravity.

F. REVERSE RAFTER ORDER

- Repeat Scenario E with opposite placement order.
- Confirm equivalent geometry and joint graph.

G. MISSING LOWER SUPPORT

- Build a valid peak with only one lower support.
- Confirm preview identifies the unresolved side.
- Test stability.
- Confirm the roof shifts or fails naturally.

H. ASYMMETRIC ROOF

- Use unequal support heights or unequal valid slopes.
- Confirm clean endpoint seam.
- Confirm no forced symmetry.
- Test stability.

I. CANDIDATE AMBIGUITY

- Position a vertical beam where Corner Joint, T-Joint, and Face Joint are all
  plausible.
- Confirm deterministic default.
- Cycle candidates.
- Confirm each preview is distinct and stable.
- Commit the selected relationship.

J. REPEATED TEST AND RESTORE

- Build a frame containing corners, rafters, peak, brace, and T-joint.
- Test and restore three times.
- Confirm body, joint, and constraint counts remain constant.
- Confirm no increasing energy.

K. PROJECTILE IMPACT

- Strike the supported roof.
- Confirm joints flex, strain, or break according to force.
- Confirm geometry remains physically meaningful.
- Confirm damage and joint failure remain separate.

L. REINFORCEMENT

- Form a corner or rafter support during reinforcement.
- Confirm same snap behavior.
- Confirm no overlap with surviving wisps.
- Confirm history remains correct.

